  "passage": "Workers cleaning a storage room found old election posters from many years ago. The faces, slogans, and colors looked outdated.\nCivics students studied them. They compared the issues on the posters with current political topics. Some concerns had changed. Others, like jobs, safety, and education, remained familiar.\nThe teacher reminded students that posters are designed to persuade, not simply inform. Students looked again and noticed large smiles, strong words, and promises without details.\nThe old posters became useful classroom tools.\nDemocracy requires more than voting. It requires reading carefully when people are trying to win your trust.",
